1
00:00:02,800 --> 00:00:07,700
For the AstraZeneca challenge, we started with Finland's national cancer roadmap.

2
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:12,500
One line stuck with us: people over 100 km from a radiotherapy unit get less palliative radiotherapy.

3
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:15,100
So: two women with the same breast cancer.

4
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:19,500
One lives in Helsinki, 9 minutes from the hospital. Home every night.

5
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:24,300
The other lives in Utsjoki. Her nearest unit is in Oulu…

6
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:27,100
…676 km away. More than 9 hours each way.

7
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:30,500
15 sessions means 16 nights away from home.

8
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:36,000
Then we looked at the evidence: two shorter schedules already backed by trials.

9
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:40,500
First, breast. If the lymph nodes don't need treating…

10
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:44,500
…5 sessions in one week is at least as good as 15 over three weeks.

11
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:47,000
FAST-Forward trial: over 4,000 patients.

12
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:49,500
Utsjoki: 16 nights away become 6.

13
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:53,500
Across Finland: about 17,500 radiotherapy sessions freed a year. Goal 3: treatment within target times.

14
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:58,500
Second, painful bone metastases: one 8 Gy session relieves pain as well as a longer course.

15
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:03,000
More people need a second treatment, and the model counts it.

16
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:07,000
Nights away still drop: 6.2 → 2.4.

17
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:12,500
The whole country. Height = nights away per patient. The north and east carry it.

18
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:18,500
With 5 sessions: 16 nights become 6.

19
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:23,000
What do hospitals do today? AI read every unit's public patient pages, checking every quote.

20
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:27,300
Only 1 of 12 units says which schedule it uses.

21
00:01:27,300 --> 00:01:31,500
So today's mix is an assumption you can change.

22
00:01:31,500 --> 00:01:37,000
To make it usable, Matka writes a memo for every county.

23
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:41,900
Lapland: 3 proposals, each with an owner and a first step in 30 days. 9 of 9 numbers traced.
